observer (0.9.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Clicking a gauge now scrolls the window to the process list and puts the
    keyboard focus in it. At the default window size the list used to open
    below the fold, and the click looked like it had done nothing: it was
    the most serious finding of the interface review.
  * A second click on the same gauge closes the list; a click on another
    gauge switches it without closing.
  * The process list has column headings - Name, CPU, Memory, I/O - and grows
    with the window instead of stopping at 260 pixels and scrolling inside a
    page that already scrolls.
  * One "End process" button that changes its label on the first click,
    instead of two buttons swapping places and taking the keyboard focus
    with them.
  * Gauges have a name and a value for screen readers, and the clickable
    ones show a hand cursor; the disk space gauges, which open nothing, no
    longer wear the faint box of a disabled button.
  * The window opens at 900x700 and cannot go below 720x520: the old minimum
    of 420x360 predated the machine list and cut the only visible gauge in
    half.
  * Captions and section titles come from the Fluent type scale and take
    their colour from the theme instead of a hand-picked opacity; the gauge
    caption never goes below 11 px.
  * Less work when nobody is looking: minimised, the dashboard reads every
    ten seconds instead of every second, and the history strips of all
    gauges are fetched together instead of one after another.

